Harbor's task cache is ~/.cache/harbor/tasks and its path is hardcoded (harbor/constants.py:
CACHE_DIR = Path("~/.cache/harbor")), so it cannot be scoped per job the way HF_HOME is.
Concurrent runs against a COLD dataset race on it and leave half-written task directories --
tests/ present, task.toml missing -- and every one of them then dies with

    Error: [(... '/home/u4320956/.cache/harbor/tasks/<hash>/<task>/task.toml',
             "[Errno 2] No such file or directory: ...")]

within two minutes, exiting 0 from the job script so it looks like a clean completion.

Warm the cache once, serially, before submitting concurrent policies on a new dataset:

    harbor datasets download 'terminal-bench@2.0' --cache

and delete any entry missing its task.toml before retrying.
